{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the bundle entries as relative symlinks that retain the targets recorded in links.tsv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both entries remain symbolic links, now point to the relative targets `releases/two` and `releases/two/report.txt`, match links.tsv, resolve successfully, and the final audit found no absolute symlinks.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6373d1fcddc945e5","cmd-4214784551da4336","cmd-dc02b94f1bad4903","cmd-6f223ce2301147b4"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Ensure the bundle works in its current location and after being copied elsewhere.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests accessed matching report content through both links in place and in temporary relocated copies, including after node restart; temporary copies were removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc02b94f1bad4903","cmd-bf7a1066657d4e9a","cmd-6f223ce2301147b4"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the bundle's regular files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final and post-restart SHA-256 hashes for both report files exactly match the prepared baseline, and the final inventory retains the original file layout, modes, and ownership.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-6373d1fcddc945e5","cmd-bf7a1066657d4e9a","cmd-6f223ce2301147b4"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 remained unchanged. The repair used the already-installed RHEL coreutils, with no evidence of package installation or replacement; package health remained good after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1663ed33d1184e7e","cmd-6373d1fcddc945e5","cmd-bf7a1066657d4e9a","cmd-6f223ce2301147b4","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The symlink replacements were the required repair (cmd-4214784551da4336). Temporary relocation copies were bounded verification artifacts and were removed (cmd-dc02b94f1bad4903, cmd-bf7a1066657d4e9a). The scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart-evidence protocol and its transient unit did not remain (cmd-a6c62acb87dd4fee, cmd-6f223ce2301147b4). The failed initial validation exited before creating its temporary directory and shows no state mutation (cmd-14d6711b5f674588). Final snapshots show no failed services, package damage, unsafe new listeners, or executor-created residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4214784551da4336","cmd-14d6711b5f674588","cmd-dc02b94f1bad4903","cmd-a6c62acb87dd4fee","cmd-bf7a1066657d4e9a","cmd-6f223ce2301147b4","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The links are relative, correct, functional both in place and after relocation, and remain symlinks; regular files, OS release, and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart scheduling, observed connection interruption, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, SSH, security, network, data, link, and relocation behavior.","limitations":[]}
